Task 1: Registering a System Subscription
Objective: Register your system with Red Hat Subscription Manager (RHSM) to access official repositories.

Step 1: Check Subscription Status
Run the following command to verify if the system is already registered:

sudo subscription-manager status
Expected Output:

If registered, it shows subscription details.
If not, it indicates "This system is not yet registered."
Step 2: Register the System
(For RHEL only, skip if using Fedora/CentOS Stream)

sudo subscription-manager register --username=<your_username> --password=<your_password> --auto-attach
Expected Outcome:

System successfully registers and attaches available subscriptions.
Troubleshooting Tip:

If registration fails, ensure network connectivity and correct credentials.
Task 2: Enabling and Disabling Repositories
Objective: Manage software repositories to control package sources.

Step 1: List Available Repositories
sudo dnf repolist all
Expected Output:

A list of enabled and disabled repositories.
Step 2: Enable a Repository
sudo dnf config-manager --enable <repo_name>
Example (for EPEL on CentOS/Fedora):

sudo dnf install epel-release -y
sudo dnf config-manager --enable epel
Step 3: Disable a Repository
sudo dnf config-manager --disable <repo_name>
Expected Outcome:

The repository status changes in dnf repolist.
Task 3: Installing, Removing, and Updating Packages
Objective: Manage individual packages using dnf.

Step 1: Install a Package
sudo dnf install -y httpd
Expected Outcome:

The httpd package is installed.
Step 2: Remove a Package
sudo dnf remove -y httpd
Expected Outcome:

The httpd package is uninstalled.
Step 3: Update Packages
sudo dnf update -y
Expected Outcome:

All installed packages are updated to the latest versions.
Task 4: Working with Package Groups and Modules
Objective: Install and manage package groups and modules.

Step 1: List Available Package Groups
sudo dnf group list
Expected Output:

A list of available package groups (e.g., "Development Tools").
Step 2: Install a Package Group
sudo dnf group install -y "Development Tools"
Expected Outcome:

All packages in the group are installed.
Step 3: List Available Modules
sudo dnf module list
Expected Output:

A list of available modules (e.g., nodejs).
Step 4: Enable and Install a Module
sudo dnf module enable -y nodejs:18
sudo dnf install -y nodejs
Expected Outcome:

The nodejs:18 module is enabled and installed.
